cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the weight diffs, please cite it as below."
title: "Blind weight edits for language confusion in Qwen3.5-0.8B and Qwen3.5-2B"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jha"
    given-names: "Ankit"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3901-0315"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "TODO-on-release"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ankit373/weight-edit-qwen"
abstract: >-
  Code for a study that asks whether Claude Opus 5.5, acting as a blind
  editor, can cut cross-lingual language confusion in Qwen3.5-0.8B and
  Qwen3.5-2B by editing their weights directly, with no training. Five
  editor runs (four on the 0.8B model, one on the 2B model) are compared
  with published training-free fixes on the Language Confusion Benchmark.
  The frozen edits are also checked on two other cross-lingual prompt
  sets, on Global-MMLU, MGSM and IFEval, under greedy decoding and longer
  answers, and with a blind LLM judge.
keywords:
  - language confusion
  - model editing
  - weight diff
  - multilingual
  - Qwen3.5
